{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"L01\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"حَتَّىٰٓ carries the motion from the preceding route into a reached endpoint; the scene opens as the next stage of travel, not as a detached tableau.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:85\",\"ar\":\"فَأَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا بَلَغَ مَغْرِبَ ٱلشَّمْسِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:90\",\"ar\":\"ثُمَّ أَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا\"}],\"activation\":\"The opening ḥattā follows the route-taking in 18:85 and introduces the arrival frame.\",\"limits\":\"The particle marks the transition to an endpoint; it does not identify the route or make the endpoint a metaphysical boundary.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"L02\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"إِذَا stages a particular arrival, with perfect بَلَغَ followed by successive findings and speech; the scene is narrated as an event rather than a habitual journey.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"إِذَا بَلَغَ مَغْرِبَ ٱلشَّمْسِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ وَوَجَدَ عِندَهَا قَوْمًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"قُلْنَا يَٰذَا ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The perfect arrival verb and the sequence of discoveries and address fill out this temporal frame.\",\"limits\":\"The frame gives the scene an eventive reading; it does not by itself settle the scope of the conditional coloring in إِذَا.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"L03\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"بَلَغَ makes the named place the reached limit of this leg of travel. Repetition at the next two stations divides Dhū al-Qarnayn’s movement into successive endpoint scenes.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"بَلَغَ مَغْرِبَ ٱلشَّمْسِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:90\",\"ar\":\"بَلَغَ مَطْلِعَ ٱلشَّمْسِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:93\",\"ar\":\"بَلَغَ بَيْنَ ٱلسَّدَّيْنِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The same verb opens each of the three station scenes, while its object changes from sunset-place to sunrise-place to the space between barriers.\",\"limits\":\"The repeated verb establishes a narrative pattern of arrival, not that the three destinations have identical significance.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L04\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"مَغْرِبَ names the setting-place in the construct مَغْرِبَ ٱلشَّمْسِ, then تَغْرُبُ repeats the same root as an action. The reached place and the sun’s disappearance are bound together in the wording.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"مَغْرِبَ ٱلشَّمْسِ وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The place noun is immediately followed by a verb from the same غ ر ب root.\",\"limits\":\"The root reprise links the destination with the setting action; it does not add an independent meaning such as exile to the passage.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"L05\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"ٱلشَّمْسِ fixes the destination as the setting-place of the known sun, and the feminine suffix in وَجَدَهَا retrieves that same noun. The eastern station later completes a west-to-east solar frame in the travel narrative.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"مَغْرِبَ ٱلشَّمْسِ وَجَدَهَا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:90\",\"ar\":\"مَطْلِعَ ٱلشَّمْسِ وَجَدَهَا تَطْلُعُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The definite sun is the genitive partner in the first construct and the most direct antecedent of هَا; the next endpoint names its rising place.\",\"limits\":\"The wording frames the journey through sunset and sunrise; it does not specify a complete itinerary between them.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L06\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"وَجَدَهَا makes the setting report a finding from the traveler’s scene: the sun is found while تَغْرُبُ. The parallel وَجَدَهَا تَطْلُعُ at the eastern station repeats this perspectival construction.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:90\",\"ar\":\"وَجَدَهَا تَطْلُعُ عَلَىٰ قَوْمٍۢ\"}],\"activation\":\"The attached feminine object is followed by a verbal clause describing the state in which the sun is found.\",\"limits\":\"This construction presents the scene as perceived at the endpoint; it does not independently settle the physical or cosmological interpretation of the image.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L07\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"تَغْرُبُ presents sunset as underway within the finding scene. The imperfect keeps the action open as the following phrase locates it in فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"تَغْرُبُ فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ\"}],\"activation\":\"The imperfect verb occurs as the setting state inside وَجَدَهَا, with a locative phrase directly after it.\",\"limits\":\"The form sustains the scene in progress; it does not establish that the setting is a recurring or habitual event.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"L08\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"فِى makes the spring-like locus part of how the sunset is seen: the verb is not left as unlocated disappearance. The preposition allows a contained scene but does not itself require a motion-into reading.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"تَغْرُبُ فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ\"}],\"activation\":\"فِى directly governs the indefinite noun عَيْنٍ and its adjective.\",\"limits\":\"Containment is supported by the phrase; direction of motion into the spring is not encoded by فِى alone.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"L09\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"عَيْنٍ names the muddy water source, while its eye or aperture sense is activated by the nearby finding and seeing scene: the place of disappearance is expressed with a word that can also name an eye.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ\"}],\"activation\":\"وَجَدَهَا and تَغْرُبُ frame a perceived disappearance, and حَمِئَةٍ describes the locus as muddy.\",\"limits\":\"The adjective and locative syntax select a spring as the phrase’s sense; they do not establish a literal eye or a second simultaneous referent.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L10\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"حَمِئَةٍ describes the spring as muddy or darkened; the supplied variant حَامِيَةٍ instead makes heat salient. The two forms alter the material image at this endpoint.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ\"}],\"activation\":\"The adjective agrees with عَيْنٍ, so the variant changes the quality assigned to the spring, not to the sun.\",\"limits\":\"The printed form here is حَمِئَةٍ; the variant does not combine mud and heat into one adjective in this wording.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L11\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"وَوَجَدَ restarts the finding with a new object: after the sun and its setting state, the traveler finds a people. This is the hinge from the horizon scene to a human encounter.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَجَدَهَا تَغْرُبُ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَوَجَدَ عِندَهَا قَوْمًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The repeated verb changes from an attached feminine object to the overt collective قَوْمًا.\",\"limits\":\"The coordination orders two discoveries; it does not state that the people witnessed the sunset.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L12\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"عِندَهَا places the people near the preceding scene, whereas the earlier فِى locates the setting within the spring. The change marks adjacency without putting the people inside the spring.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ وَوَجَدَ عِندَهَا قَوْمًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The locative follows the sunset-in-a-spring phrase and introduces the second finding.\",\"limits\":\"The suffix هَا can point to the spring or to the wider scene; the wording does not resolve its precise antecedent.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L13\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"قَوْمًا enters as the overt object of the second finding, a collective treated as a group. The following options concern that group, with them understood as the object of تُعَذِّبَ and stated as the domain in فِيهِمْ.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"وَوَجَدَ عِندَهَا قَوْمًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"إِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ حُسْنًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The collective object is followed directly by options about treatment, one with an implied object and one with an explicit plural suffix.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not identify this people or specify their prior conduct here.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L14\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"قُلْنَا changes the narrative into direct divine address, placing the two courses of action within an authorized decision frame for Dhū al-Qarnayn.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"قُلْنَا يَٰذَا ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ إِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:87\",\"ar\":\"قَالَ أَمَّا مَن ظَلَمَ فَسَوْفَ نُعَذِّبُهُۥ\"}],\"activation\":\"The first-person plural speech verb introduces a vocative and second-person options; the next verse gives his response.\",\"limits\":\"The verb establishes who speaks in the narrative frame; it does not alone specify how the authority was communicated.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L15\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"يَٰ opens a vocative before the title and before either course is stated, directing the alternatives to a named addressee.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"قُلْنَا يَٰذَا ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ إِمَّا\"}],\"activation\":\"The address sits between the divine speech verb and the paired options.\",\"limits\":\"The vocative focuses the address but adds no separate instruction about which option to choose.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"L16\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The dual form ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ sits immediately before إِمَّا … وَإِمَّا, giving the title’s grammatical twoness a formal echo in the two branches.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"يَٰذَا ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ إِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The dual title and the paired alternatives occur consecutively in the same address.\",\"limits\":\"The adjacency supports a formal echo; it does not assign one branch to each of the title’s two parts or establish the title’s intended etymology.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L17\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The first إِمَّا opens a choice whose paired second branch prevents تُعَذِّبَ from reading as a standalone command. The second-person form leaves the addressee as the agent of either course.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"إِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:87\",\"ar\":\"قَالَ أَمَّا مَن ظَلَمَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The repeated disjunctive frame and Dhū al-Qarnayn’s ensuing reply make the first action one available branch.\",\"limits\":\"The form offers alternatives but does not by itself explain why one branch would be chosen for a particular person.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L18\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The first أَن places تُعَذِّبَ under the first option; its repetition before تَتَّخِذَ gives the two actions matching grammatical packaging.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"إِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both option particles are followed by أَن and a subjunctive verb.\",\"limits\":\"The parallel syntax balances the alternatives formally without making their moral content equivalent.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"L19\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"تُعَذِّبَ assigns the first punitive action to the addressed ruler, with قَوْمًا recoverable as its object. The next verse shifts to first-person plural punishment and then the Lord’s punishment, placing earthly action within a larger judgment.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"قَوْمًۭا قُلْنَا يَٰذَا ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ إِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:87\",\"ar\":\"فَسَوْفَ نُعَذِّبُهُۥ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِۦ فَيُعَذِّبُهُۥ\"}],\"activation\":\"The second-person singular verb is answered by a response that names a first punishment and then a return to the Lord.\",\"limits\":\"The sequence establishes distinct agents and stages; it does not specify the legal form or severity of Dhū al-Qarnayn’s action.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L20\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"وَإِمَّا introduces the second branch as the counterpart to punishment, completing the either-or frame rather than adding a second action to the first.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"أَن تُعَذِّبَ وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ حُسْنًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The particle repeats the first إِمَّا after وَ and introduces a differently directed course.\",\"limits\":\"The paired form establishes alternatives; the reason for choosing either is developed in the following reply.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"L21\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The second أَن mirrors the first complementizer, so adopting goodness is packaged as an option on the same syntactic level as punishment.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"إِمَّآ أَن تُعَذِّبَ وَإِمَّآ أَن تَتَّخِذَ\"}],\"activation\":\"Each branch has أَن followed by a subjunctive second-person verb.\",\"limits\":\"Formal symmetry does not make the two courses interchangeable in meaning or outcome.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"L22\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"تَتَّخِذَ has حُسْنًا as its object while فِيهِمْ marks the social domain: the offered course is to adopt goodness among or toward the people, not to take the people as the object. Elsewhere in the surah the verb takes concrete objects such as a mosque or gods.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"أَن تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:15\",\"ar\":\"ٱتَّخَذُوا۟ مِن دُونِهِۦٓ ءَالِهَةًۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:21\",\"ar\":\"لَنَتَّخِذَنَّ عَلَيْهِم مَّسْجِدًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The prepositional phrase and abstract object differ from the surah’s examples where a concrete entity follows the verb.\",\"limits\":\"The wording identifies goodness as the adopted course but leaves its specific practices unstated.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L23\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"فِيهِمْ marks the people as the field or concern of the adopted goodness. It also shifts فِى from the physical spring phrase to a social domain.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"فِى عَيْنٍ حَمِئَةٍۢ وَوَجَدَ عِندَهَا قَوْمًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ حُسْنًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The same preposition first locates the sunset and later introduces the people as the domain of the second option.\",\"limits\":\"فِيهِمْ can be heard as among or concerning them; the phrase does not specify a particular policy or recipient-by-recipient distribution.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"L24\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"حُسْنًا is the direct object naming an indefinite, open-ended good course. The same root appears in the response as ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ, linking the offered treatment to the believer’s good recompense without equating the two phrases.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:86\",\"ar\":\"تَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:88\",\"ar\":\"فَلَهُۥ جَزَآءً ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ\"}],\"activation\":\"The indefinite object completes the second option, and the following answer uses the same root for a reward.\",\"limits\":\"The shared root links goodness of conduct and goodness of recompense; it does not establish that the adopted course and the reward are identical.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
